Z||000001||theogre||12-07-2001||11:44 PM||||Actually, that's not the radiator. It's the AC condensor.<P>Something hit the thing in one spot. so what.... <P>Is it running hot or something? If it is and that's the only spot like that then somthing else is wrong.<P>If it's lost the refrigerant then it will need to be replaced.<P>For most people I recomend leave a single spot like that alone. If you aren't careful you can do more harm than good trying to straighten the Aluminum fins.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroRacer||12-07-2001||11:53 PM||||You mean I won't need a new Radiator?<P>I really need to look at what I'm taking pictures of in the future, and no more night time pictures like this.||||reg||10
Z||000003||cadaver||12-08-2001||02:02 AM||||No you wont need a new radiator because of what is shown in the pic. ITS NOT THE RADIATOR. ITS THE CONDENSER. And no you dont need a new one of those either.||||reg||1
